=== PARITY (vs web RateLimitStatusPanel.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> useSystem/useRateLimitStatus (GET /system/rate-limits, the 30s pause-on-hidden poll). The
    web component owns this hook; the native surface binds the coalesced query snapshot through the P1/S8
    RateLimitSource seam (isLoading/isFetching/error/response + isStale/isOffline). The view performs NO
    HTTP. useTranslation -> the P1/S10 RLStrings facade.
  Projection -> RateLimitProjection.resolve is a 1:1 port of the web ladder
    `isLoading ? loading : error ? error : scopes.length===0 ? empty : data`; error deliberately takes
    precedence over cached rows (web shows the error box, not the stale data, on a refetch failure).
    RateLimitRowProjection.make ports the per-row useMemo maths: max=limit>0?limit:1, fraction clamped
    0…1, refill = reset_at-now dropped when nonpositive/non-finite, window phrasing flag, detail/meta
    visibility. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Composition -> the web GlassPanel: an always-visible header (panel title + subtitle + "Updated {when}"
    via formatRelative + ghost Refresh w/ fetching spinner) above the state body: loading(spinner+bodySm
    text) · error(danger box + warning triangle + retry) · empty(italic secondary text) · data(one
    RateLimitRowView per scope). Each row reproduces the web RateLimitRow: name + toned severity caption,
    a labeled TSMetricBar (window label left, monospace usage readout right, proportion bar tinted by
    severity), and the detail/“Refills in …” bottom-meta. Severity hex map (ok #10b981 / warn #f59e0b /
    critical #ef4444) -> shared TSTone .success/.warning/.danger.
  Shared components -> @/components/ui -> TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel), TSButton variant .ghost (web
